  "body": "<html><head><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"></head><body><pre>{\"data\":{\"chsHedgingFeed\":{\"name\":\"CHS Hedging RSS Feeds\",\"lastRefreshedAt\":\"2026-10-17T22:30:01.266-04:00\",\"morningHighlights\":[{\"id\":236,\"title\":\"Morning Highlights 10.16.2026\",\"author\":\"CHS Hedging\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/morning-highlights/morning-highlights/2026/10/16/morning-highlights-10.16.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;President Trump called Ukraine’s attacks on Russian oil infrastructure a “disgrace,” and said Zelensky is “more difficult to deal with than Putin.” Ukraine has seen limitations to its military-grade Starlink satellite system this week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;When asked about the “mother of all bombs,” Trump noted that it is not nuclear and that he won’t use nuclear weapons and doesn’t expect to use any U.S. ground troops in Iran.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Iran has reportedly been able to export 4.1 million barrels of LPG through the U.S. blockade since July, but crude oil exports fell to zero in September.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. September Industrial Production is expected to show a 1% increase.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of 6:55 am CT, crude oil is up 0.45 at $98.42/barrel, gold is up 23.9 at $4194.0, DOW is down 8 at 52,422, U.S. dollar index down 370, and Euro up 440 pts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly corn export sales are estimated at 600k MT – 1.2 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Expana lowered their EU corn production estimate from 46.2 MMT to 44.9 MMT, which would be the lowest since 1990.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Conab estimates the Brazilian corn crop at 148 MMT vs a 147.2 MMT average trade estimate.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December corn down 2 ½ to up 3 overnight.. corn traded to a fresh weekly low but is still around 5 cents above the WASDE report day low.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly soybean export sales are estimated at 500k MT – 1.2 MMT, soymeal sales 200k-450k MT, and soyoil sales 0-10k MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Abiove says Brazilian soybean oil production could reach 12.8 MMT in 2026 and exports 1.8 MMT. January-August bean oil exports were 1.57 MMT, already exceeding total 2025 exports of 1.36 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Overnight, China’s Dalian No2 soybeans were down 18, soymeal down 5.50, and soyoil down 59. Malaysian palm oil futures were up 1.2%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Conab estimates the Brazilian soybean crop at 181.6 MMT vs a 181 MMT average trade estimate.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div&gt;Outlook&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;November soybeans down 5 ½ to up 2 ¾ overnight.. beans are nearing a 50% retracement of their August to September rally, which would be around 12.50 for November futures. Meal is leading soy products lower, with Dec down 4.9 at 354.9.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly wheat export sales are estimated at 300k-600k MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;China set its lower tariff wheat import quota for 2027 at 9.64 MMT, unchanged from last year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Expana kept its EU wheat production estimate unchanged at 126.1 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December KC wheat&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; down 9 to up ¼ overnight.. Chicago wheat traded to its lowest since 8/12/26 as funds continue to pile on.&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-10-16T08:01:11.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"f8a622ef-0bc3-4854-9cca-09434a052012\",\"kind\":\"morningHighlights\"},{\"id\":235,\"title\":\"Morning Highlights 10.15.2026\",\"author\":\"CHS Hedging\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/morning-highlights/morning-highlights/2026/10/15/morning-highlights-10.15.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. September PPI will be released at 7:30am CT and is expected to show prices up 0.6% month-over-month and up 5.5% year-over-year. Retail sales are expected to rise 0.3% from last month. Weekly jobless claims are expected to come in at 199,000.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;CNN reports that the U.S. military is considering using the Massive Ordnance Air Blast Bomb in Iran. It is nicknamed the “mother of all bombs” and was last used in 2017 in Afghanistan.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Ukraine says it will resume attacks on Russian energy infrastructure, after Russia failed to uphold Trump’s proposed energy ceasefire.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Rabobank says EU milk production could decline by 2% year-over-year in Q4.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of 7:00 am CT, crude oil is up 0.34 at $95.43/barrel, gold is up 58.0 at $4165.9, DOW is up 100 at 51,958, U.S. dollar index down 500, and Euro up 525 pts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Widespread rains will likely slow down harvest over much of the Corn Belt today, but then the forecast dries out until the end of next week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Zimbabwe’s government says their 2027 corn production could fall 30% to 1.6 MMT due to El Nino. They are setting aside a $500 million cash and gain reserve to limit the impact.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Guizhou Origin is launching a “stress-tolerant corn breeding project” in Southwest China, targeting a +10% increase in yield and 15% reduction in pesticide and fertilizer use.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December corn up 2 to down 2 ¾ overnight.. corn futures remain stuck and are working on another inside day.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Amspec reported October 1-15 Malaysian palm oil exports up 58.3% from last month at 785,564 MT, and ITS reported 802,481 MT, up 43.2%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Overnight, China’s Dalian No2 soybeans were down 22 ¼, soymeal down 4.40, and soyoil down 76. Malaysian palm oil futures were down 1.6%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;There were 10 soyoil deliveries, now up to 459 for the month.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div&gt;Outlook&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;November soybeans down 9 ½ to unchanged overnight.. beans dropped to their lowest level since 8/27/26 as yields continue to impress. Meal is leading products higher, with December futures up 3.4 at 367.9.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Jordan is tendering for up to 120,000 MT of feed barley, with offers due October 21.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Iraq plans to procure up to 4 MMT of domestic wheat in 2026/27, up from 3.2 MMT in the previous season.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December KC wheat&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; up 2 ¼ to down 6 overnight.. wheat is finding its footing, down just 4 cents on the week so far.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-10-15T08:05:26.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"1c540917-bc7c-415f-b3bf-27747019c214\",\"kind\":\"morningHighlights\"},{\"id\":234,\"title\":\"Morning Highlights 10.14.2026\",\"author\":\"CHS Hedging\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/morning-highlights/morning-highlights/2026/10/14/morning-highlights-10.14.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The U.S. September CPI report will be released at 7:30am CT and is expected to show inflation up 0.6% from last month and up 3.6% from last year, with core inflation up 2.5%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The MBA average U.S. 30-year fixed mortgage rate is up to 7.5%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The IEA expects diesel shortages to last into the latter half of 2027.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Australia’s Bureau of Meteorology says average weekly sea-surface temperatures are hitting record highs in the central Pacific Ocean, topping the 2015 El Nino.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of 6:30 am CT, crude oil is up 1.74 at $95.88/barrel, gold is down 15.3 at $4162.0, DOW is up 141 at 52,076, U.S. dollar index up 62, and Euro down 105 pts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;France’s farm ministry cut their corn crop estimate from 8.1 MMT to 7.3 MMT, lowest on record.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Dr Cordonnier raised his U.S. corn yield estimate by 3 bushels per acre to 180.0 bpa.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Crop Progress showed corn conditions up 2 pts to 56% good-to-excellent vs a 54% average estimate. Harvest is 33% complete vs 39% average.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December corn up ¼ to down 3 ½ overnight.. corn is working on another inside day as the market comes to terms with higher production.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;China is believed to have bought 8-10 U.S. soybean cargos yesterday. They also announced another auction from state reserves for 504k MT of beans next week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Overnight, China’s Dalian No2 soybeans were up 7 ¾, soymeal flat, and soyoil up 48. Malaysian palm oil futures were up 0.36%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Dr Cordonnier raised his U.S. soybean yield estimate by 1.6 bpa to 53.1 bpa.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Crop Progress showed soybean conditions unchanged at 57% g/e. Harvest is 46% complete vs 50% average.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Soyoil open interest was up 11,520 contracts yesterday.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div&gt;Outlook&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;November soybeans up 6 ¼ to down 2 ¼ overnight.. beans are bouncing back to their 10-day moving average, after China finally returned to the export market. Soy products are slightly higher, but board crush is tracking a few cents lower.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Jordan is tendering to buy 120,000 MT of optional origin milling wheat.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Algeria bought 600k MT of 11.5 protein wheat at $326/MT C&amp;amp;F.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Winter wheat planting is 51% complete vs 58% average.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December KC wheat&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; down 7 ¼ to up 1 ¼ overnight.. wheat continues to probe lower despite the export market activity.&lt;/div&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-10-14T07:36:40.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"7902d0b3-d253-419d-a474-972892326ae1\",\"kind\":\"morningHighlights\"},{\"id\":233,\"title\":\"Morning Highlights 10.13.2026\",\"author\":\"CHS Hedging\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/morning-highlights/morning-highlights/2026/10/13/morning-highlights-10.13.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;President Trump says he is considering joining Saudia Arabia in strikes on Houthi rebels, after an attack on the Saudi Riyadh airport over the weekend. The Houthis threatened the U.S. with a “swift and painful” response. Trump says he does not believe China and Russia are helping Iran, saying they have “too much to lose.”&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Saudi Arabia says its oil production rose to 8.4 million barrels/day in September, highest since the Iran War started and up from 6.24 million bpd in August.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Russian Deputy Prime Minister Novak says Russia has the “capacity to increase diesel fuel exports” beyond what was announced by President Trump, up to 3.0-3.5 MMT per month.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;South Korea’s stock market index KOSPI was down 5.5% overnight to its lowest since August 10.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Export inspections will be released today at 10am CT, delayed a day due to Columbus Day.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of 7:00 am CT, crude oil is down 1.35 at $92.39/barrel, gold is up 18.7 at $4209.3, DOW is up 393 at 52,503, U.S. dollar index down 315, and Euro up 320 pts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Buenos Aires Grains Exchange says Argentinian corn was 29.9% planted as of Oct 8.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Ukraine’s Ministry of Agrarian Policy says corn harvest is 13% complete at 3.486 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Corn open interest was down 24,690 contracts yesterday.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December corn down 5 to up 1 overnight.. corn is trading inside yesterday’s range so far and between 100 and 200 day moving averages. RSI is at 35.33. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;MPOB palm oil stocks hit a record high in September at 3.51 MMT vs a 3.37 MMT estimate, up from 2.82 MMT in August. Production was up 16% while exports fell 12%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Ukrainian soybean harvest is 73% complete at 2.56 MMT, and sunflower harvest is 66% complete at 7.439 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Rabobank estimates Australia’s 26/27 canola crop at 8.1 MMT, up 5.3% from last year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Overnight, China’s Dalian No2 soybeans were down 11 ¾, soymeal down 1.30, and soyoil down 31. Malaysian palm oil futures were down 0.97%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;There were 51 soybean oil deliveries.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Soymeal open interest was up 11,360 contracts yesterday.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div&gt;Outlook&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;November soybeans down 12 ½ to down ½ overnight.. beans are under pressure and losing ground to corn again. Meal is giving back much of yesterday’s gains, with December down 6.9 at 361.8. December bean oil is up 0.54 at 69.17.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Rabobank sees 2026/27 Australian wheat production falling 13.3% from last year to 31 MMT, and barley production falling 1.2% to 16.5 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Ukraine has harvested 37.144 MMT of grain so far this year, with an average yield of 49.1 c/ha, up from 33.032 MMT and 43 c/ha a year ago.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December KC wheat&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; down 7 ¼ to up 1 ½ overnight.. wheat traded under last week’s low, as high world supplies weigh on the market. RSI is at 35.61.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-10-13T08:13:02.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"9aeff777-7bd0-49c8-9f19-6d629b002502\",\"kind\":\"morningHighlights\"},{\"id\":238,\"title\":\"Morning Highlights 10.12.2026\",\"author\":\"CHS Hedging\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/morning-highlights/morning-highlights/2026/10/12/morning-highlights-10.12.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Ukrainian President Zelensky accused Russia of violating their energy ceasefire by attacking a thermal power plant. He also criticized Trump’s deal to release Russian diesel and said Ukraine has “influence over whether these ships can sail or not.” Trump in response said, “I suggest they get a new leader who can make a deal.”&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Russia will release roughly 35.8 million barrels of diesel, which is 9 days of U.S. diesel demand according to EIA.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The U.S. bond market and banks are closed in observance of Columbus Day, while equities and commodities remain open.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Today is day 4 of the Goldman index roll.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of 6:45 am CT, crude oil is up 1.34 at $93.19/barrel, gold is down 22.1 at $4194.2, DOW is up 54 at 51,980, U.S. dollar index up 218, and Euro down 265 pts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;China’s Ag Ministry lowered their 2026/27 corn consumption estimate from 311.7 MMT to 306.9 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Eurostat and DG AGRI estimate EU corn production at 50.2 MMT, down 12% from last year and down 18% from their 2015-2024 average.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;CME corn futures saw record volume of 1,203,000 contracts on Friday.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Commitments of Traders for the week ended 10/6/26 showed funds sold 60,491 corn and were still long 317,359 contracts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December corn up 2 ¾ to down 3 ¾ overnight.. corn is steady, finding support at its 200-day moving average after Friday’s big drop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Zambia shipped their first cargo of soybeans to China on October 10. The countries have had a phytosanitary agreement since 2024.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Overnight, China’s Dalian No2 soybeans were down 1 ¼, soymeal down 0.80, an soyoil up 9. Malaysian palm oil futures were down 1%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;GAPKI says Indonesia’s palm oil exports could fall by 15% in 2027 to 26.5 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;FAS expects Vietnam to increase their soybean imports in 26/27 from 3.8 MMT to 4 MMT as new crush capacity coming online.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Commitments of Traders showed funds bought 10,496 soybeans and were long 251,660 contracts. They also bought 11,572 soyoil, long 99,447 contracts, and sold 612 soymeal, long 206,804 contracts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div&gt;Outlook&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;November soybeans down 14 to down 2 ¾ overnight.. beans gapped lower after weathering the WASDE storm on Friday. The 2027 bean/corn ratio is back down to 2.4577. December bean oil is up 0.38 to start, despite lower diesel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Ukraine’s Zelensky said at the Warsaw Security Forum, “Everyone is talking about diesel, but no one is talking about grain – there will be a crisis in 2-3 months.”&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Algeria is tendering to buy at least 50k MT of optional origin milling wheat for December shipment.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Commitments of Traders showed funds sold 7,873 Chicago wheat, short 29,543 contracts, sold 6,670 KC wheat, long 24,040 contracts, and Sold 4,537 Minneapolis wheat, long 11,669 contracts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;div class=\\\"mb-3\\\"&gt;Outlook: &nbsp;December KC wheat&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt; up 3 to down 8 overnight.. wheat is gauging the ceasefire prospects between Russia and Ukraine, after futures fell to their lowest since mid-July on Friday.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-10-12T07:50:18.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"dd839a24-b15d-499d-a7c1-b8e6a21c8d90\",\"kind\":\"morningHighlights\"}],\"afternoonHighlights\":[{\"id\":107,\"title\":\"Afternoon Highlights 8.6.2026\",\"author\":\"Chad Pater\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/afternoon-highlights/afternoon-highlights/2026/08/06/afternoon-highlights-8.6.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Corn and soybeans managed to finish slightly higher, even as wheat markets posted steep declines.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;While the U.S. and Iran have yet to reach a deal, details of a framework agreement between Iran and Oman were announced, leaving the U.S. on the sidelines. The news helped support a rebound in energy markets, which moved higher today.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Forecasts issued at midday turned a bit drier for the Western Corn Belt during the next one to five days.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Senate Agriculture Committee failed to advance the 2026 Farm Bill after an 11-11 party-line vote, with SNAP funding emerging as the primary point of contention.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. jobless claims remained low, underscoring continued labor market strength. Initial claims rose slightly to 199,000 but came in below expectations, while continuing claims increased to 1.801 million, indicating it’s taking unemployed workers longer to find a new job.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of this writing, the U.S. dollar index is up 0.304 to 99.850 points, crude oil is up $2.73 to $77.95 per barrel, the E-mini S&amp;amp;P is down 19.75 to 7,729.75, and gold is down 3.80, trading at $4,242.00 per ounce.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Corn ended the day with modest gains following a choppy session and a more favorable weather forecast.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly corn export sales were reported this morning, with 25/26 commitments reaching 116,700 MT and new‑crop bookings totaling 1,026,900 MT.&nbsp; Average estimates for all marketing years were 1,350,000 MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;In today’s drought monitor map for the week ending August 4, corn acres in drought are at 28%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The CU26/CZ26 carry closed at 22 ½¢, CZ26/CH27 carry closed at 15 ¾¢. &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;This morning's daily export sales announcements showed that private exporters reported sales of 122,000 metric tons of soybeans to China for delivery in the 2026/27 marketing year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;USDA flash sales over the last two weeks have reached roughly 70 million bushels, led by strong demand from China.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;July Malaysian palm oil futures were down 16 ringgit overnight, closing at 4,686.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly export sales:&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;25/26 soybeans totaled 32,200 MT, and 26/27 totaled 903,900 MT. Estimates for all marketing years were just shy of 1.5 MMT.&nbsp; &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Soymeal sales reached 101,400 MT for the 25/26 marketing year and 146,700 MT for 26/27, while average estimates were 350,000 MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Soybean oil net sales totaled 3,900 MT for 25/26, and zero new-crop (26/27) sales were reported, falling above overall expectations.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\\n&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;In today’s drought monitor map for the week ending August 4, soybean acres in drought is at 26%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;SU26/SU26 is at a 18¢carry, SX26/SF27 is at a 15¢ carry. &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;September SRW finished below its 100-day moving average today, leaving the market vulnerable as it looks for technical support.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;This morning’s weekly wheat export sales report showed 26/27 commitments at 296,400 MT, sales came in below the average estimate of 350,000 MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Spring wheat acres affected by drought for the week ending August 4 is 42%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;WU26/WZ26 is at 19 ¼¢ carry, KWU26/KWZ26 is at 18¢ carry, and MWU26/MWZ26 is at 23 ¼¢ carry.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-08-06T16:33:55.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"17f1be7a-128f-4cdc-99e6-e10728e50b1a\",\"kind\":\"afternoonHighlights\"},{\"id\":106,\"title\":\"Afternoon Highlights 8.5.2026\",\"author\":\"Chad Pater\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/afternoon-highlights/afternoon-highlights/2026/08/05/afternoon-highlights-8.5.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Grain futures were mixed today, with corn, soybeans, and nearby Minneapolis wheat moving lower, while Chicago and Kansas City wheat contracts posted gains.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;According to the EIA, the U.S. Strategic Petroleum Reserve posted its 19th straight weekly decline, reaching its lowest level since February 1983.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Dow Jones Industrial Average is trading higher mid-afternoon, while the S&amp;amp;P 500 and Nasdaq are lower.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Market participants are beginning to focus on the August 12 USDA WASDE report, as consensus estimates are expected to be released late this week or early next week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. mortgage rates continued to edge higher, with the average 30-year fixed rate increasing to 6.81% from 6.76% last week.&nbsp; This is the highest this print has been in almost a year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The ADP Employment Report indicated the U.S. economy added 44,000 jobs, a weaker-than-expected reading that missed consensus forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of this writing, the U.S. dollar futures index is down 0.169 to 99.570 pts, crude oil is down $0.71 to $75.06 per barrel, the S&amp;amp;P 500 futures are down 10.25 to 7,755.25, and gold is up $157.00, trading at $4,252.40 per ounce.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The corn market reacted to Monday's two-point decline in the crop's good-to-excellent rating, with futures ending lower for the second consecutive day.&nbsp; Rain and cooling temperatures have kept pressure on prices.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;A total of 120,000 metric tons of corn were sold to Mexico by private exporters for delivery, 90,000 MT in the 2026/27 marketing year, 30,000MT in the 2027/28 marketing year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;According to the EIA, ethanol production declined by 26,000 barrels per day to 1.107 million bpd, closely matching trade expectations for a decrease of 25,000 bpd. The four-week average stood at 1.094 million bpd.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. gasoline consumption decreased by 10,000 bpd to 9.031 million bpd. The four-week average is 8.966 million bpd.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The CU26/CZ26 carry is 23¢. &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;According to the World Meteorological Organization, El Niño continues to strengthen and is expected to persist through October 2026, increasing the likelihood of above-normal temperatures across much of the globe and contributing to significant shifts in rainfall patterns.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. biodiesel exports totaled 34,507 metric tons in June, up from 19,448 metric tons in May and just below the 35,081 metric tons exported in June of last year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The EIA reported Wednesday that U.S. commercial crude oil production roseby 8,000 bpd at 13.804 million bpd. A year ago, production totaled 13.284 million bpd during the same period.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Malaysian palm oil futures rose 6 ringgit to close at 4,702.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;SU26/SZ26 closed at a 18¢ carry, SX26/SF27 is at a 15¢ carry.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Wheat received support today from solid global demand and persistent export uncertainty in the Black Sea region.&nbsp; SovEcon reported July wheat exports reached a nine-year low for the month.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Jordan has issued a new tender to purchase up to 120,000 metric tons of optional origin milling wheat.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;EU soft wheat exports continue to trail last year's pace, totaling 700,000 metric tons so far in the 2026/27 marketing year, compared with 1.79 million metric tons at this point a year ago.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;WN26/WU26 is at 18 ¾¢ carry, KWN26/KWU26 is at 17 ½¢ carry, and MWN26/MWU26 is at 24 ½¢ carry.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-08-05T16:33:12.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"b002471d-1f63-4441-a041-464d1503c893\",\"kind\":\"afternoonHighlights\"},{\"id\":105,\"title\":\"Afternoon Highlights 8.4.2026\",\"author\":\"Chad Pater\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/afternoon-highlights/afternoon-highlights/2026/08/04/afternoon-highlights-8.4.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The market narrative today is one of stark contrast, grain and energy futures are moving lower, while financial markets are rallying aggressively and pushing to new highs.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Market participants are beginning to focus on the August 12 USDA WASDE report, as consensus estimates are expected to be released late this week or early next week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;According to President Trump, the U.S. and Iran remain in active talks, which he described as Iran's last chance to secure a deal. The negotiations are reportedly focused on restoring access through the Strait of Hormuz and resolving issues related to Iran's nuclear ambitions.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Looking ahead, the 2026 Pro Farmer Crop Tour begins in roughly two weeks and will take place August 17-20.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;In yesterday’s crop progress report, the USDA continues to have corn, soybeans, and wheat developing ahead of last year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of this writing, the U.S. dollar futures index is down 0.041 to 99.740 pts, crude oil is down 4.61 to $75.73 per barrel, the S&amp;amp;P 500 futures are up 152.0 to 7,780.25, and gold is up $54.40, trading at $4,088.10 per ounce.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Most of the Corn Belt is expected to receive above-normal rainfall in the 6-to-14-day forecast, putting additional pressure on the grain markets.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Total New World screwworm detections in the U.S. held steady at 44 cases today, the same as reported yesterday.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Dr. Cordonnier kept his corn yield forecast to 181 bushels per acre this week.&nbsp; High temperatures were buffered by scattered rainfall.&nbsp; &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The CU26/CZ26 carry closed at 23 ¼¢, and the CZ26/CH27 carry closed at 15 ¾¢.&nbsp; &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;A total of 132,000 metric tons of soybeans were sold to China by private exporters for delivery in the 2026/27 marketing year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Dr. Cordonnier left his U.S. soybean yield estimates at 52.0 bpa again this week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Maritime workers in Argentina have launched a strike that is blocking ships from accessing the country's grain ports, disrupting operations and slowing activity at a major export hub.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Palm oil futures were stronger Tuesday, gaining 67 ringgits.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;SU26/SX26 spread is inverted 18 ¾¢, the SX26/SF27 is at a 15 ¼¢ carry.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Spring wheat harvest advanced to 5% complete versus 2% last week, though it continues to trail the 8% average pace. Crop ratings improved slightly, with 55% of the crop rated good-to-excellent, up from 53% a week ago.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Several South Korean flour mills jointly bought about 50,000 MT of various U.S. wheat classes in a recent tender.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The USDA attaché in Canada estimates the 2026 wheat crop at 34.6 MMT, marginally higher than the USDA’s official forecast, but production remains significantly below last year’s 40.0 MMT crop.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;WU26/WZ26 is at a 18 ½¢ carry, KWU26/KWZ26 is at a 17 ¼¢ carry, and MWU26/MWZ26 is at a 24 ¾¢ carry.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-08-04T17:08:59.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"c4ef740d-438b-4d39-a269-cd7b86f9b305\",\"kind\":\"afternoonHighlights\"},{\"id\":104,\"title\":\"Afternoon Highlights 7.24.2026\",\"author\":\"Chad Pater\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/afternoon-highlights/afternoon-highlights/2026/07/24/afternoon-highlights-7.24.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. forces conducted a 13th consecutive night of strikes against Iranian military targets, as reports emerged of additional Iranian drone and missile attacks targeting U.S. bases in Kuwait and Jordan.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;After the prior 10% global tariff expired, the U.S. introduced new Section 301 duties of 10% to 12.5% on imports from about 60 countries, citing forced labor concerns.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Extreme heat is set to return to the Northern Plains this weekend and continue into next week, while the 7-day forecast shows increased chances for rainfall across the eastern U.S.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;First Notice Day for August futures is Friday, July 31. Be out of longs by the close of business on Thursday, July 30 or risk participating in the delivery process.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of this writing, the U.S. dollar index is up 0.029 to 101.315 pts, crude oil is down $2.08 to $90.11 per barrel, the E-mini S&amp;amp;P is down 0.50 to 7,444.50, and gold is up $21.40, trading at $4,068.00 per ounce.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The NWS website still lists 42 confirmed New World screwworm detections nationwide, with 10 active cases remaining, all concentrated in Texas.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;December corn futures closed the week unchanged on Friday, for the week, December corn ended 20 cents higher.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;FranceAgriMer's latest report showed the corn crop rated 38% good-to-excellent, down 2 points from the previous week and well below 69% a year earlier.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Disaggregated Commitment of Traders report released Friday after the market close for the week ending July 21 showed that managed money was a net buyers of corn contracts, being net long 92,909, up 49,518 this week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The CU26/CZ26 carry closed at 23 ½¢, CZ26/CH27 carry closed at 15 ½¢.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;November soybeans gained 9 ¾ cents on Friday, bringing the weekly gain to 50 ½ cents.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Disaggregated Commitment of Traders report released Friday for the week ending July 21 showed managed money increasing their net long to 124,900, a 52,212 contract increase in soybeans.&nbsp; They also increased their net long position in soybean oil 12,319 to 125,348.&nbsp; Their net long soybean meal position also increased to 75,152, a 27,300 contract gain.&nbsp; &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;According to Rabobank, Brazil’s 2026/27 soybean production is projected at 178 MMT, down 2% year over year from 2025/26.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Palm oil futures were stronger Friday, gaining 12 ringgits and closed up 125 ringgits for the week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;SQ26/SZ26 closed inverted by 7 ¾¢, SX26/SF27 is at a 13 ¾¢ carry.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Wheat Quality Council released the final results of its Hard Red Spring Wheat Tour, reporting a three-day weighted average yield of 48.0 bushels per acre from 238 surveyed fields.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;September wheat posted losses across all exchanges Friday:&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Chicago wheat lost 18 ¼ cents Friday and was down 4 ¾ cents for the week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Kansas City wheat dropped 14 ½ cents Friday and was up 13 cents for the week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Minneapolis wheat fell 15 ¾ cents on Friday but was up 22 ½ cents for the week.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\\n&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Russian consultancy IKAR reduced its wheat production forecast to 90.0 million metric tons, compared with its earlier projection of 91.5 MMT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The Disaggregated Commitment of Traders report for the week ending July 21 showed that managed money was:&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;A net buyer of 17,449 contracts of SRW this week to end at a net short of 19,349.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;HRS was a net buyer for the week of 8,237 contracts to end the week at a net long of 2,525.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;HRW was also a net buyer of 12,450 contracts to close the week at a net long of 29,944.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\\n&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;WU26/WZ26 is at 17 ¾¢ carry, KWU26/KWZ26 is at 16 ¼¢ carry, and MWU26/MWZ26 is at 23 ½¢ carry.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-24T16:38:07.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"1a72f25f-e606-4554-a0f7-a4b385a181ce\",\"kind\":\"afternoonHighlights\"},{\"id\":103,\"title\":\"Afternoon Highlights 7.23.2026\",\"author\":\"Chad Pater\",\"link\":\"https://chshedging.com/insights/afternoon-highlights/afternoon-highlights/2026/07/23/afternoon-highlights-7.23.2026\",\"desc\":\"&lt;h3&gt;Highlights&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Middle East tensions remained elevated, with the U.S. conducting strikes against Iran for a 12th straight night, while Iran backed Houthi forces in Yemen reportedly targeted two Saudi oil tankers in the Red Sea using drones.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;U.S. equities were sharply lower in Thursday afternoon trading, with the Dow Jones Industrial Average, S&amp;amp;P 500, and Nasdaq all posting significant declines.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rose to 4.71%, its highest level in roughly 18 months, reflecting market expectations that the Federal Reserve's next policy move could be an interest rate increase rather than a rate cut.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Initial jobless claims came in much lower than expected this morning, with initial jobless claims coming in at 187,000 for the week ending July 18.&nbsp; The market was expecting jobless claims to come in roughly at 211,000 to 212,000.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;As of this writing, the U.S. dollar index is up 0.341 to 101.295 points, crude oil is up $5.07 to $91.90 per barrel, the E-mini S&amp;amp;P is down 107.50 to 7,432.75, and gold is down 100.30, trading at $4,046.60 per ounce.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Corn&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly corn export sales were reported this morning, with 25/26 commitments reaching 332,700 MT and new‑crop bookings totaling 701,500 MT.&nbsp; Estimates for all marketing years were 800,000 to 1,600,000 MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;In today’s drought monitor map for the week ending July 21, corn acres in drought increased to 20%, up 1% from last week. At this time last year, the total was 9%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;September Brent crude surpassed $100 per barrel, reflecting the strongest price level seen in nearly two months.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;The CU26/CZ26 carry closed at 23 ¾¢, CZ26/CH27 carry closed at 15 1/2¢. &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Oilseeds&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;This morning's daily export sales announcements showed that private exporters reported sales of 126,000 metric tons of soybeans to unknown for delivery in the 2026/27 marketing year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;USDA reported a private export sale of 126,000 metric tons of soybeans to unknown destinations for delivery during the 2026/27 marketing year.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;July Malaysian palm oil futures were up 88 ringgits overnight, closing at 4,710.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Weekly export sales:&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;25/26 soybeans totaled 56,400 MT, and 26/27 totaled 1,537,200 MT. Estimates for all marketing years were 1,200,000 to 2,200,000 MT.&nbsp; &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Soymeal sales reached 185,000 MT for the 25/26 marketing year and 406,100 MT for 26/27, while estimates were 100,000 to 575,000 MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Soybean oil net sales totaled 600 MT for 25/26, with 1,100 MT new-crop (26/27) sales reported, falling within expectations.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\\n&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;In today’s drought monitor map for the week ending July 21, soybean acres in drought stayed at 18%, the same as last week. Last year, the figure stood at 8%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;SQ26/SU26 is inverted 6 ¾¢, SX26/SF27 is at a 13¢ carry. &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4 class=\\\"mt-2\\\"&gt;Wheat&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Wheat Quality Council Spring Wheat &amp;amp; Durum Tour Day 2 results point to slightly improved spring wheat and durum yield potential compared to a year ago.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Scouts surveyed 108 fields across northwest and north-central North Dakota, estimating an average yield of 48.1 bpa, up from 46.2 bpa on Day 2 of last year's tour. &lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;This morning’s weekly wheat export sales report showed 26/27 commitments at 290,000 MT, sales came in at the bottom of the estimates range of 200,000 to 550,000 MT.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;India increased its wheat purchasing program to 34.5 MMT from 30 MMT, aiming to strengthen government stockpiles and provide additional market support for domestic wheat farmers.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;Spring wheat acres affected by drought rose to 25% this week, up 1% from last week. &nbsp;Last year at this time the figure stood at 43%.&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;li&gt;WU26/WZ26 is at 17 ½¢ carry, KWU26/KWZ26 is at 16¢ carry, and MWU26/MWZ26 is at 23¢ carry.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;\\n&lt;/ul&gt;\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T15:21:26.000-04:00\",\"uuid\":\"0b5427fd-07bb-4bcf-978b-232519f9409f\",\"kind\":\"afternoonHighlights\"}]}}}</pre><div class=\"json-formatter-container\"></div></body></html>"
 },
 {
